      "text_unit_id": "tu_0002",
      "verbatim_text": "In patients with chronic or recurrent hyperkalaemia not on maximal tolerated guideline-recommended target dose of RAAS inhibitors, an approved $K^+$ -lowering agent may be initiated as soon as confirmed $K^+$ levels are $>5.0$ mEq/L. Closely monitor $K^+$ levels. Maintain treatment unless alternative treatable aetiology is identified. RAAS inhibitors should be optimized when $K^+$ levels are $<5.0$ mEq/L."
