      "text_unit_id": "tu_0003",
      "verbatim_text": "In patients with $K^+$ levels of $4.5$ – $5.0$ mEq/L not on maximal tolerated, guideline-recommended target dose of RAAS inhibitor therapy, RAAS inhibitor therapy can be initiated/up-titrated with a close monitoring of $K^+$ levels. If $K^+$ levels rise above $5.0$ mEq/L, initiate an approved $K^+$ -lowering agent."
